      en: "Xi'an is the capital of Shaanxi Province in central China, one of the oldest cities with over 3,000 years of history. It served as the capital for 13 dynasties, including the Qin, Han, and Tang. Xi'an is world-famous for the Terracotta Army, discovered in 1974, featuring thousands of life-sized clay soldiers. The city also boasts a well-preserved Ming Dynasty city wall. Xi'an is a major cultural and educational hub, with numerous universities and research institutes. It was the eastern terminus of the Silk Road. Local cuisine, such as Biangbiang noodles and lamb paomo, is renowned. The city's Muslim Quarter reflects its historical diversity.",
