      en: "Shenyang, the capital of Liaoning Province, is the industrial and cultural center of northeast China. With over 8 million inhabitants, it has a significant history as the capital of the Qing Dynasty before the conquest of Beijing. The city houses the Shenyang Imperial Palace, a UNESCO World Heritage site. Shenyang is known for its heavy industry, particularly machinery and automobile manufacturing. The 9.18 Historical Museum commemorates the Mukden Incident. The city has a well-preserved old town district with traditional architecture.",
